WEBVTT

00:00:24.144 --> 00:00:27.147
Why did you never tell me
about my father?
你怎么从不说我父亲的事？

00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:34.696
My mother was a Black Dwarf
from the Northern Mountains.
我母亲是北方山峦的黑矮人

00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:39.451
I risked my life all these years
我这些年冒险

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:43.205
so that one day...
只为了有一天

00:00:43.288 --> 00:00:47.334
...you might be a better king
than those before you.
你能成为比你祖先更好的王

00:00:50.003 --> 00:00:52.297
Then I have failed you.
那么我让你失望了

00:00:55.884 --> 00:01:00.722
Everything I told you...
everything I didn't...
我告诉你和没告诉你的一切

00:01:00.806 --> 00:01:04.684
...it was only because I believe in you.
都只是因为我相信你

00:01:04.768 --> 00:01:10.732
You have a chance to become
the most noble contradiction in history.
你有机会成为
历史上最高贵的矛盾

00:01:14.027 --> 00:01:17.364
The Telmarine who saved Narnia.
拯救纳尼亚的坦摩人

00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:44.057
You're lucky, you know.
你很幸运

00:01:45.892 --> 00:01:47.853
What do you mean?
什么意思？

00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:51.314
To have seen him.
能够看到他

00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:57.696
I wish he'd just given me
some sort of proof.
我真希望他能给我们一些证明

00:02:00.157 --> 00:02:03.785
Maybe we're the ones who need
to prove ourselves to him.
也许我们应该证明给他看

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:11.668
Pete. You'd better come quickly.
彼得 你最好快点过来

00:03:14.648 --> 00:03:18.276
Cakes and kettledrums.
That's your next big plan?
我的老天爷
这就是你下一个伟大的计划？

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.907
Sending a little girl into
the darkest parts of the forest? Alone!
派小女孩去黑森林的深处？
一个人去！

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:27.911
- It's our only chance.
- And she won't be alone.
这是我们唯一的机会
她也不会是一个人去

00:03:29.996 --> 00:03:33.750
Haven't enough of us died already?
我们死的人还不够多吗？

00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:38.255
Nikabrik was my friend too.
But he lost hope.
尼卡不里也曾是我的朋友
不过他失去了希望

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.008
Queen Lucy hasn't.
And neither have I.
露西女王没有 我也没有

00:03:43.134 --> 00:03:45.095
For Aslan.
为了亚斯蓝

00:03:45.178 --> 00:03:46.680
For Aslan!
为了亚斯蓝

00:03:51.643 --> 00:03:55.230
- Then I'm going with you.
- No. We need you here.
那我跟你一起去
不 我们需要你在这里

00:03:55.313 --> 00:03:57.691
We have to hold them off
until Lucy and Susan get back.
我们要撑着等露西和苏珊回来

00:03:59.317 --> 00:04:00.860
(Caspian) If I may...
我有个建议

00:04:05.532 --> 00:04:09.703
Miraz may be a tyrant and a murderer...
米拉兹也许是暴君和凶手

00:04:11.454 --> 00:04:16.209
...but as king, he is
subject to the traditions...
不过身为国王必需遵循传统

00:04:16.293 --> 00:04:20.130
...and expectations of his people.
以及人民的期望

00:04:20.213 --> 00:04:24.009
There is one in particular
that may buy us some time.
有个方法
也许能帮我们拖点时间

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.978
Perhaps they intend to surrender.
也许他们想投降

00:04:35.061 --> 00:04:36.563
No.
不

00:04:39.107 --> 00:04:42.152
They are much too noble for that.
他们太高尚 不会投降

00:04:43.862 --> 00:04:48.325
"I, Peter, by the gift of Aslan,
by election and by conquest,
我 彼得 奉亚斯蓝赐命
经推选与指定

00:04:48.408 --> 00:04:53.538
High King of Narnia, Lord of Cair
Paravel and emperor of the Lone Islands,
纳尼亚之王
凯尔帕拉瓦领主以及寂岛皇帝

00:04:53.622 --> 00:04:56.166
in order to prevent the
abominable effusion of blood,
为免流血杀戮

00:04:56.249 --> 00:05:01.421
do hereby challenge the usurper Miraz to
single combat upon the field of battle.
特此向篡位者米拉兹
挑战进行一场比武战斗

00:05:01.504 --> 00:05:06.635
The fight shall be to the death.
The reward shall be total surrender."
比武以性命为赌注奖赏
是败方的全面投降

00:05:09.638 --> 00:05:11.973
- Tell me, Prince Edmund...
- King.
告诉我 爱德蒙王子
国王

00:05:12.057 --> 00:05:17.270
- Pardon me?
- It's "King Edmund," actually.
什么？
其实是爱德蒙王

00:05:17.354 --> 00:05:20.023
Just "King," though.
Peter's the high king.
只有“王”
彼得才是真正的国王

00:05:20.106 --> 00:05:22.942
I know, it's confusing.
我知道 这有点乱

00:05:25.528 --> 00:05:28.365
Why would we risk such a proposal
我们的军队能一举歼灭你们

00:05:28.448 --> 00:05:31.868
when our armies could
wipe you out by nightfall?
我为何要冒险接受这种提议？

00:05:33.203 --> 00:05:35.872
Haven't you already
underestimated our numbers?
你是不是低估我们的人数了？

00:05:35.955 --> 00:05:41.544
I mean, only a week ago
Narnians were extinct.
一星期前纳尼亚人还绝迹了呢

00:05:41.628 --> 00:05:43.838
And so you will be again.
这下你们就等着绝迹吧

00:05:43.922 --> 00:05:46.174
Then you should have little to fear.
那么你就没什么好怕的了

00:05:46.257 --> 00:05:50.178
(laughing) This is not
a question of bravery.
这不是怕不怕的问题

00:05:50.261 --> 00:05:53.932
So you're bravely refusing to fight
a swordsman half your age?
所以你勇敢的拒绝
跟一位少年武士比武？

00:05:55.975 --> 00:05:59.145
I didn't say I refused.
我没说我拒绝

00:05:59.229 --> 00:06:01.690
(man) You have our support,
Your Majesty.
我们支持你 陛下

00:06:01.773 --> 00:06:03.566
Whatever your decision.
不论你的决定为何

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:08.613
Sire, our military advantage alone
provides the perfect excuse to avoid
陛下 我们的军事优势
是最充足的理由

00:06:08.697 --> 00:06:11.741
- what might otherwise be...
- I'm not avoiding anything!
避免不必要的…
我没有避免什么

00:06:13.368 --> 00:06:14.994
I was merely pointing out
我只是想指出

00:06:15.078 --> 00:06:17.914
that my lord is well
within his rights to refuse.
陛下有权拒绝比武

00:06:17.997 --> 00:06:20.500
His Majesty would never refuse.
陛下绝不会拒绝

00:06:21.584 --> 00:06:24.295
He relishes the chance
to show the people
他喜欢把握机会

00:06:24.379 --> 00:06:26.673
the courage
of their new king.
向人民展现新国王的勇气

00:06:31.845 --> 00:06:32.929
You.
你

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:41.479
You should hope your brother's sword
is sharper than his pen.
你最好希望你哥哥的剑
比他的笔还要锋利

00:06:46.192 --> 00:06:50.572
Destrier has always served me
well. You are in good hands.
戴斯奇一直很照顾我
他会与你们好好携手合作

00:06:50.655 --> 00:06:52.323
Or hooves.
你是说蹄吧

00:06:57.203 --> 00:07:01.207
- Good luck.
- Thanks.
祝好运
谢了

00:07:05.879 --> 00:07:07.297
Look.
听着

00:07:08.548 --> 00:07:11.342
Maybe it is time you had this back.
也许你该拿回这个了

00:07:13.887 --> 00:07:18.349
Why don't you hold on to it.
You might need to call me again.
何不由你来保管它呢
你可能会需要再找我

00:07:25.398 --> 00:07:27.609
(Lucy) You might need
to call me again?
你可能会需要再找我？
闭嘴啦

00:07:27.692 --> 00:07:29.486
(Susan) Oh, shut up.
你可能会需要再找我？
闭嘴啦

00:07:31.821 --> 00:07:34.908
(crowd cheering, shouting)

